Guard the null menu bar in wxApp::OSXOnBuildMenu (iPhone).

This is the SIGSEGV that stopped every wx iOS app from reaching OnInit.
Backtrace, from the wx probe (run 16):

    2  wxMenuBar::OSXOnBuildMenu(NSObject*) + 376      <- fault
    3  wxApp::OSXOnBuildMenu(NSObject*)
    4  -[wxAppDelegate buildMenuWithBuilder:]
    5  -[UIMenuSystem _buildMenuWithBuilder:fromResponderChain:...]
    8  -[UIMainMenuSystem _automaticallyRebuildIfNeeded]
   11  -[UIApplication _immediatelyUpdateSerializableKeyCommands]
   12  -[_UIAfterCACommitBlock run]
   22  UIApplicationMain

wxApp::OSXOnBuildMenu dereferences MacGetInstalledMenuBar() unconditionally,
and that returns s_macInstalledMenuBar, which is nullptr until some wxMenuBar
has actually been installed. wxMenuBar::OSXOnBuildMenu then walks
m_rootMenu->GetMenuItems() through a null this, and the process is gone.

UIKit builds the main menu from an after-CA-commit block during the first turn
of the run loop, to populate the key-command table. On iPadOS that happens
whether or not the application has any menus, and it happens before OnInit has
run - so an app that installs its menu bar in OnInit, and every app that never
installs one at all, is dereferencing null.

Two things in this port make it reachable. Patch 0202 turns wxUSE_MENUBAR on for
the iPhone build, which is what compiles the buildMenuWithBuilder: delegate
method into existence at all; Orca's MainFrame needs the class, so that flag has
to stay. And patch 0208 hands OnInit to the next turn of the main queue, which
puts UIKit's first menu build firmly ahead of it. The step-2 smoke app -- a
frame, a button and a GL canvas, with no menus anywhere -- crashes identically,
which is what makes this a wx bug rather than an Orca one.

Doing nothing when no menu bar is installed is also the right behaviour on its
own terms: there is nothing to contribute to the builder, and UIKit's defaults
are what should remain.

diff --git a/src/osx/carbon/app.cpp b/src/osx/carbon/app.cpp
--- a/src/osx/carbon/app.cpp
+++ b/src/osx/carbon/app.cpp
@@ -244,7 +244,17 @@

 void wxApp::OSXOnBuildMenu(WX_NSObject builder)
 {
-    wxMenuBar::MacGetInstalledMenuBar()->OSXOnBuildMenu(builder);
+    // UIKit rebuilds the main menu from an after-CA-commit block on the first
+    // turn of the run loop, to fill in the key-command table, and it does so
+    // before the application's OnInit has had a chance to install anything.
+    // MacGetInstalledMenuBar() is null until a wxMenuBar is installed, and it
+    // stays null for the whole life of an app that never uses menus, so this
+    // dereference is a startup segfault rather than an edge case.
+    wxMenuBar* const menubar = wxMenuBar::MacGetInstalledMenuBar();
+    if ( menubar == nullptr )
+        return;
+
+    menubar->OSXOnBuildMenu(builder);
 }

 #endif
